    b" `from_*`\x0aconstructor scales in exact arbitrary-precision arithmetic, accepts a\x0a"
    b"negative argument, and cannot overflow.\x0a\x0aDeliberately narrower than `Temporal.Du"
    b"ration` (TC39): there are no\x0ayear/month/week/day fields, only nanoseconds. Calen"
    b"dar units are the part of\x0aTemporal's duration model that cannot be interpreted w"
    b"ithout a reference\x0apoint \xe2\x80\x94 a month is 28 to 31 days, and a day is not 24 hours"
    b" on the dates a\x0azone shifts. Omitting them keeps every `Duration` operation exac"
    b"t. The\x0aconsequence: adding a 24-hour `Duration` to a `ZonedDateTime` advances th"
    b"e\x0aabsolute time by exactly 24 hours, which is not \"the same wall-clock time\x0atomo"
    b"rrow\" across a DST transition.\x0a\x0aEvery `to_*` accessor below is lossy except `to_"
    b"nanoseconds`. Each truncates\x0atoward zero rather than flooring, so a negative `Du"
    b"ration` rounds up: -1500\x0ananoseconds reads back as -1 microsecond, not -2.\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00j"
