    b"baml.Array.filled\x00\x00\x00\x00\x01!\x03\x00\x00Returns an array of `length` elements, every one of th"
    b"em `value`.\x0a\x0aThe idiomatic way to allocate a runtime-sized, pre-initialized buff"
    b"er \xe2\x80\x94\x0aFenwick trees, DP tables, adjacency lists \xe2\x80\x94 without a `while`/`push`\x0alo"
    b"op.\x0a\x0aEvery slot holds that one `value`, so for a reference type all slots\x0aalias "
    b"the same object and mutating one slot mutates them all. Use\x0a`Array.generate` for"
    b" an independent value per slot.\x0a\x0a# Parameters\x0a- `length`: how many elements to c"
    b"reate. Zero or negative produces an\x0a  empty array.\x0a- `value`: the value stored i"
    b"n every slot.\x0a\x0a# Examples\x0a```baml\x0aArray.filled(3, 0)     // [0, 0, 0]\x0aArray.fill"
    b"ed(-1, 0)    // []\x0a\x0alet shared: int[] = [];\x0alet rows = Array.filled(3, shared); "
