    b"ml.Array.generate\x1e\x00\x00\x00<builtin>/baml/containers.baml\x01\\\x03\x00\x00Returns an array of `len"
    b"gth` elements, where element `i` is `f(i)`.\x0a\x0aUnlike `Array.filled`, which reuses"
    b" one shared value, every slot gets an\x0aindependent value \xe2\x80\x94 the alias-free way t"
    b"o build runtime-sized buffers of\x0areference types, such as the rows of a grid. Th"
    b"is is JavaScript's\x0a[`Array.from({ length }, f)`](https://developer.mozilla.org/e"
    b"n-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Array/from)\x0aand a Python list "
    b"comprehension.\x0a\x0a# Parameters\x0a- `length`: how many elements to create. Zero or ne"
    b"gative produces an\x0a  empty array and never calls `f`.\x0a- `f`: called once per ind"
    b"ex `0, 1, \xe2\x80\xa6, length - 1`, in order, to produce\x0a  that slot's value.\x0a\x0a# Example"
    b"s\x0a```baml\x0aArray.generate(3, (i: int) -> int { i * i })      // [0, 1, 4]\x0a// A 2D"
