    b"ds a TCP listener on `addr` and returns a `Server` ready to `serve`.\x0a`\":0\"` (e.g"
    b". `\"127.0.0.1:0\"`) asks the OS for an ephemeral port; the chosen\x0aaddress is avai"
    b"lable as `.addr`. The socket starts queuing incoming\x0aconnections immediately, so"
    b" a client may connect before `serve` is called.\x0a\x0a# Parameters\x0a- `addr`: The addr"
    b"ess to bind. E.g. `\"127.0.0.1:8080\"` or `\"127.0.0.1:0\"`.\x01\x04\x00\x00\x00bind\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00"
