    b"\x0e\x01\x00\x00\x00\x1e\x00\x16\x00\x00\x00baml.http.Server.serve\"\x00\x00\x00<builtin>/baml/ns_http/server.baml\x01P\x0b\x00\x00Serv"
    b"es requests with `handler`, blocking the current thread until it is\x0acancelled. T"
    b"o run it in the background, use `spawn { server.serve(...) }`.\x0a\x0aEach incoming re"
    b"quest is dispatched on its own BAML thread, so requests are\x0ahandled concurrently"
    b" (including multiplexed HTTP/2 streams on one\x0aconnection). Each request is isola"
    b"ted: if the `handler` panics or its\x0aresponse can't be written (e.g. a client tha"
    b"t hung up early), only that\x0arequest fails \xe2\x80\x94 the client receives a `500` and th"
    b"e server keeps serving.\x0a\x0aA `Server` serves one handler at a time: calling `serve"
    b"` while it is already\x0aserving raises `Io`. Once a serve ends (its thread is canc"
    b"elled), the same\x0a`Server` may be served again \xe2\x80\x94 with a different `handler`, `t"
    b"ls_config`, or\x0aprotocol set if desired. The bound port is held until the `Server"
    b"` itself is\x0adropped, not when a serve ends.\x0a\x0a# Parameters\x0a- `handler`: Turns eac"
    b"h incoming `Request` into a `Response`.\x0a- `websocket`: Handles WebSocket upgrade"
    b" requests (see `WsAccept`). Returning a\x0a  `Response` refuses the upgrade and ser"
    b"ves that response; returning a `WsAccept`\x0a  completes the handshake and runs it "
    b"with the connected socket. The default\x0a  refuses every upgrade with `501`.\x0a- `tl"
    b"s_config`: Optional TLS configuration. If provided, the server behaves as an HTT"
    b"PS server.\x0a- `allow_http1` / `allow_http2`: Which HTTP versions to accept (at le"
    b"ast one must be true).\x0a- `max_body_size`: Maximum request body size, in bytes, b"
    b"uffered per request\x0a  (default 100 MiB). A larger body is rejected with `413 Pay"
    b"load Too Large`,\x0a  bounding per-request memory.\x0a- `max_connections`: Maximum num"
    b"ber of connections served concurrently\x0a  (default 1024). At the cap the accept l"
    b"oop applies backpressure (new\x0a  connections wait in the kernel backlog) rather t"
    b"han spawning unbounded tasks.\x0a  An accepted WebSocket holds its slot for as long"
    b" as the socket lives, not\x0a  just for the handshake.\x0a- `header_read_timeout`: How"
    b" long a client has to send the complete request\x0a  headers before the connection "
    b"is closed (default 30s) \xe2\x80\x94 a Slowloris defense.\x0a  A non-positive duration disab"
    b"les it. (HTTP/1 only; HTTP/2 frames its headers.)\x0a\x0a# WebSockets\x0aA request is dis"
    b"patched to `websocket` instead of `handler` only when it is a\x0acomplete RFC 6455 "
    b"handshake \xe2\x80\x94 an HTTP/1.1 `GET` carrying `Connection: Upgrade`,\x0a`Upgrade: websoc"
    b"ket`, and `Sec-WebSocket-Version: 13`. Anything short of that,\x0aincluding WebSock"
    b"et over HTTP/2 (RFC 8441 extended CONNECT, unsupported here),\x0ais an ordinary req"
    b"uest and goes to `handler`.\x0a\x0aThe handshake response is built by the server, so a"
    b" `WsAccept` cannot add\x0aheaders to it: `Sec-WebSocket-Protocol` subprotocols and "
    b"extensions are not\x0anegotiated.\x0a\x0a# Panics\x0a- Calling `serve` on an unsupported pla"
    b"tform (e.g. in the browser) will panic.\x0a- If the serving thread is cancelled, `s"
    b"erve` ends with a\x0a  `baml.panics.Cancelled` panic and any in-flight connections "
    b"are dropped.\x01\x05\x00\x00\x00serve\x09\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x005\x00\x00\x00\x01\x03\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x12\x00\x0f\x03\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x01\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00"
