    b".to_zoned)\x00\x00\x00<builtin>/baml/ns_time/plaindatetime.baml\x014\x07\x00\x00Locates this wall-clo"
    b"ck reading in a timezone, producing an absolute\x0atime. The counterpart of `ZonedD"
    b"ateTime.to_plain`.\x0a\x0aWith a `TimeZoneOffset` the conversion is exact arithmetic: "
    b"a fixed\x0aoffset has no transitions, every civil reading maps to exactly one\x0ainsta"
    b"nt, and none of the failures below can arise. With an IANA\x0aidentifier it is a lo"
    b"okup in the host's timezone database, and that\x0amapping is not total \xe2\x80\x94 a spring"
    b"-forward transition leaves a *gap* of\x0areadings that never happened, and a fall-b"
    b"ack transition leaves an\x0a*overlap* of readings that happened twice. `disambiguat"
    b"ion` decides what\x0ato do at both.\x0a\x0a# Parameters\x0a\x0a- `timezone`: a `TimeZoneOffset`"
    b" for a fixed offset, or an IANA\x0a  identifier such as `\"America/Los_Angeles\"`.\x0a- "
    b"`disambiguation`: how to resolve a DST gap or overlap; see\x0a  `Disambiguation`. D"
    b"efaults to `\"compatible\"` and, being defaulted, is\x0a  named-only: `dt.to_zoned(tz"
    b", disambiguation = \"earlier\")`. Ignored for\x0a  a `TimeZoneOffset`, which can neve"
    b"r be ambiguous.\x0a\x0a# Returns\x0a\x0aA `ZonedDateTime` carrying the resolved absolute tim"
    b"e and the timezone\x0aas given \xe2\x80\x94 an IANA identifier stays an identifier, so the v"
    b"alue keeps\x0atracking that zone's future transitions rather than freezing today's\x0a"
    b"offset.\x0a\x0a# Throws\x0a\x0a- `baml.time.UnknownTimezoneError` if `timezone` is a string "
    b"the host's\x0a  timezone database does not know.\x0a- `baml.time.AmbiguousTimeError` i"
    b"f `disambiguation` is `\"reject\"` and\x0a  the reading falls in a gap or an overlap."
    b"\x0a- `baml.errors.Io` if the host's timezone database fails to resolve the\x0a  readi"
    b"ng, including when the civil value is outside the year range the\x0a  host can repr"
    b"esent.\x0a\x0a# Panics\x0a\x0a- `baml.panics.HostUnavailable` if the host has no timezone da"
    b"tabase at\x0a  all. An unknown identifier is an error because the caller chose the\x0a"
    b"  identifier; a missing database is a property of the platform.\x01\x08\x00\x00\x00to_zoned\x03\x00\x00\x00"
