    b"<builtin>/baml/ns_time/zoneddatetime.baml\x01\xfb\x05\x00\x00Creates a `ZonedDateTime` from cal"
    b"endar and clock components read in\x0a`timezone` \xe2\x80\x94 i.e. from a wall-clock reading"
    b" someone in that zone would\x0agive you.\x0a\x0aEquivalent to building a `PlainDateTime` "
    b"from the same components and\x0acalling `to_zoned` on it, and it inherits that meth"
    b"od's DST handling.\x0a\x0aEvery clock component and `disambiguation` are defaulted and"
    b" therefore\x0anamed-only: `ZonedDateTime.from_components(tz, 1979, 5, 27, hour = 7)"
    b"`.\x0a\x0a# Parameters\x0a\x0a- `timezone`: a `TimeZoneOffset` for a fixed offset, or an IAN"
    b"A\x0a  identifier. Leads rather than trails the components because the\x0a  components"
    b" are meaningless without it.\x0a- `year`: the proleptic Gregorian year, in `[-9999,"
    b" 9999]`.\x0a- `month`: 1-based, in `[1, 12]`.\x0a- `day`: 1-based, and must exist in t"
    b"hat month of that year.\x0a- `hour`: in `[0, 23]`.\x0a- `minute`, `second`: each in `["
    b"0, 59]`.\x0a- `millisecond`, `microsecond`, `nanosecond`: each in `[0, 999]`, and\x0a "
    b" each an independent digit group.\x0a- `disambiguation`: how to resolve a DST gap o"
