    b"R\x05\x00\x00Make one run's journal safe to replay to `client_id`, and return the\x0asanitiz"
    b"ed copy. Every client should lower\x0a`ai.wire.sanitize_for_client(input.journal, s"
    b"elf.id())` instead of\x0a`input.journal`. The rules, in the order they apply per ev"
    b"ent:\x0a\x0a 1. An assistant turn from a DIFFERENT `client_id` loses its\x0a    `ai.conte"
    b"nt.Reasoning` blocks: one model's thinking is not replayable\x0a    to another (and"
    b" providers that check reasoning signatures reject it).\x0a 2. Empty and whitespace-"
    b"only `ai.content.Text` blocks are dropped from\x0a    assistant turns.\x0a 3. An assis"
    b"tant turn left with no blocks at all is dropped entirely \xe2\x80\x94\x0a    the reasoning-o"
    b"nly turn that lowers to `content: []` and makes\x0a    Anthropic 400, and the same "
    b"shape an aborted turn leaves behind.\x0a    Such a turn never has tool calls, so no"
    b"thing is orphaned by dropping it.\x0a 4. A tool call with no `ToolCompleted`/`ToolF"
    b"ailed` before the next\x0a    assistant or user message (or before the end of the j"
    b"ournal) gets a\x0a    synthesized `ToolFailed { message: \"No result provided\" }`, b"
    b"ecause\x0a    most APIs reject a tool call that was never answered.\x0a\x0aJournal-only e"
    b"vents (`RunStarted`, `ToolRequested`, `Usage`,\x0a`FinalProduced`) pass through unt"
    b"ouched \xe2\x80\x94 clients skip them anyway \xe2\x80\x94 and,\x0alike the clients' own lowering, the"
    b"y never close an open tool-result group.\x0aNothing here mutates the journal it is "
    b"given.\x01\x13\x00\x00\x00sanitize_for_client\x02\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x10\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x84\x00\x00\x00G\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00*\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x02\x03\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00\x00G\x01\x00"
