    b"openai/ns_internal/chat.baml\x01\xfd\x02\x00\x00`ai.Journal` -> chat-completions messages. Assi"
    b"stant turns carry their text\x0ain `content` and their calls in `tool_calls`; each "
    b"result comes back as its\x0aown `role: \"tool\"` message keyed by `tool_call_id`. Jou"
    b"rnal-only events\x0a(`RunStarted`, `ToolRequested`, `Usage`, `FinalProduced`) and r"
    b"easoning\x0ablocks lower to nothing.\x0a\x0aCallers pass the journal through `ai.wire.san"
    b"itize_for_client` first, so\x0aforeign reasoning, empty turns and unanswered tool c"
    b"alls are already handled.\x0a\x0aA journal turn's text always collapses to a bare stri"
    b"ng (`_chat_content`\x0awith `collapse = true`): a text-only turn was always sent th"
    b"at way, and a\x0abare string is the one content shape every compatible server accep"
    b"ts. A\x0aturn carrying media, or a user turn carrying `metadata`, is a part list.\x01\x12"
