    b"s_internal/messages.baml\x01w\x04\x00\x00(internal) Drop null-valued map entries, recursivel"
    b"y. BAML serializes an unset optional\x0afield as an explicit `null`, which the Mess"
    b"ages API rejects for several\x0aparameters; the typed request classes above therefo"
    b"re go through this on\x0atheir way to the wire, which is exactly serde's `skip_seri"
    b"alizing_if =\x0a\"Option::is_none\"` in the Rust builders this replaces.\x0a\x0aNulls INSID"
    b"E arrays are preserved (a JSON Schema `\"enum\": [null]` survives),\x0aand the two OP"
    b"AQUE subtrees below are copied verbatim. The passthrough merge \xe2\x80\x94\x0awhere `null` "
    b"means \"delete this key\" \xe2\x80\x94 still runs AFTER this, on the\x0aalready-pruned base.\x0a\x0a"
    b"`input` (a replayed tool call's arguments) and `input_schema` (a tool's JSON\x0aSch"
    b"ema) are user/model JSON whose keys are DATA, not request parameters: a\x0anull the"
    b"re means \"the model answered null\" / `\"default\": null`, not \"unset\x0aoption\". Prun"
    b"ing them rewrote conversation history on replay \xe2\x80\x94 every optional\x0atool paramete"
    b"r the model answered with null silently vanished from the\x0areplayed tool_use, and"
